{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "002B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$y$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$x \\to y$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$y$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0011": "$y \\to x$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-initial-final}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3dd18fe1cf7ed5e8865adbd181e5590004d80c6abdaa435ed2828a4baddb1ca4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:29dd67ed1de0bd2b4bfd5d7e35bd6594a3119cb487d303500b307accdbb6e950", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> An object <MATH_0002> of the category <MATH_0003> is called\nan <TEXTITOPEN_0001>initial<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> object if for every object <MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005>\nthere is exactly one morphism <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0003> An object <MATH_0007> of the category <MATH_0008> is called\na <TEXTITOPEN_0002>final<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> object if for every object <MATH_0009> of <MATH_0010>\nthere is exactly one morphism <MATH_0011>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cb9ea5cd788486ffe221dfa1bbdfcb3764aa9d9908371c13c9bdd62d8a564cc6", "unit_id": "tag:002C:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "002B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\emptyset$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b75750d760531005fd2771c7fcb3f425ae7d32b6ba21da5f32177ebde51402f9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a2f7f605ae1fe3dc7c37176ee2236816f4a313d44111d5ce54de9fdf0c82a513", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the category of sets the empty set <MATH_0001> is an\ninitial object, and in fact the only initial object.\nAlso, any <TEXTITOPEN_0001>singleton<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, i.e., a set with one element,\nis a final object (so it is not unique).", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a54dadd5a113d238d33d3a63fe1635f7970474b408206ccda0b8e27f9d1407bb", "unit_id": "tag:002B:paragraph-0001"}
